---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy"
  summary="What information this site collects, why, and your rights."
  updated="2 October 2026"
>
  <div class="page-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>In short:</strong> this site uses no cookies, does not ask for your name or contact
      details, and does not sell or share personal information. It counts visits anonymously so
      we can see which pages are useful.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Better Leasehold is responsible for the information described on this page. You can reach us
    through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>

  <h3>Visitor statistics</h3>
  <p>
    We use <a href="https://umami.is" rel="noopener">Umami</a> to count visits. It records which
    pages are viewed, how far down a page visitors scroll, the referring website, and general
    details such as browser, device type and country.
  </p>
  <p>
    Umami does not use cookies and does not store your IP address. It cannot identify you or
    follow you across other websites.
  </p>

  <h3>Server logs</h3>
  <p>
    Like almost every website, our hosting provider automatically keeps short-term logs of
    requests to the site, including IP addresses. These are used to keep the site secure and
    working, and are deleted after a limited period.
  </p>

  <h3>The eligibility checker</h3>
  <p>
    Your answers to the eligibility checker stay in your browser. They are never sent to us or
    stored. If visitor statistics are enabled, we may count that the checker was used, but never
    your answers alongside who you are.
  </p>

  <h3>If you contact us</h3>
  <p>
    If you email us, we use your message and email address only to reply and to deal with your
    enquiry. We keep it only as long as needed for that purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <p>
    We rely on our legitimate interests in running a secure website and understanding which
    guidance is useful, in a way that has minimal impact on your privacy. Where you contact us,
    we use your details to respond to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell or share personal information. Our hosting provider and Umami process data on
    our behalf, only to provide their services.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>tell you what personal information we hold about you and give you a copy</li>
    <li>correct information that is wrong</li>
    <li>delete your information</li>
    <li>stop or limit how we use it</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To make a request, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. If you are unhappy with how
    we handle your information, you can complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">Information Commissioner’s Office</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page if what we collect changes. The date at the top shows when it was
    last updated.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
